ent process includes technical review/publication approvals\n- repo_access: +1 — docs repos accessible\n- architecture_claims: 0\n\nNow file naming for signals: `artifacts/epic-tasks/{ID}-ENNN-ai-signals.md` and `{ID}-BRANCH-<letter>-ENNN-ai-signals.md`.\n\nNow, frontmatter set commands. Note dependencies format: \"RHAISTRAT-9008-E002\" as comma-separated list. gated_by=E002 id. gate_failure_impact.action and gate_failure_impact.fallback_approach.\n\nFor E005: dependencies=RHAISTRAT-9008-E002, gated_by=RHAISTRAT-9008-E002, gate_failure_impact.action=rewrite, fallback=\"If the onboarding definition lands scope elsewhere, this epic's scope is rewritten around the defined scope; Dashboard-side onboarding steps are expected to exist in any product-UI scope.\"\n\nE006: action=remove, fallback=\"If the defined onboarding scope does not include the workbench experience, this epic is dropped and onboarding work is absorbed by the Dashboard-side implementation.\"\n\nE007: action=rewrite, fallback=\"If the tooling investigation identifies specific tools, this epic is rewritten around them; if no actionable tools are identified, the epic is removed and HLR-3 is closed as not actionable.\"\n\nBranch A: branch=A gated_by=RHAISTRAT-9008-E001 dependencies=RHAISTRAT-9008-E001 gate_failure_impact.action=remove fallback=\"If the investigation selects fine-grained controls (or a layered approach that subsumes simplification), this branch is dropped in favor of the per-project controls branch.\"\n\nHmm wait — layered approach = both branches execute. So fallback for A: \"If the simplification direction is not selected, this branch is dropped in favor of the per-project controls branch; under a layered outcome both branches are planned.\" OK.\n\nBranch B similar.\n\nE008: dependencies=RHAISTRAT-9008-E001,RHAISTRAT-9008-E005,RHAISTRAT-9008-E006,RHAISTRAT-9008-E007. implementation_type=docs-authoring. No gated_by (not gated by an investigation per se... it's not \"downstream of investigat