{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-881ec5d0-15bb-4db7-8f86-b041307495fd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b206e992baf1f054","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9008-fqg9annm/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9008-E001.md","content":"# Resolve conflicting administration-usability direction for enterprise accounts\n\n## Description\n\nHLR-1 asks that \"administration should be simpler\", but the consolidated\naccount feedback is directly contradictory: one strategic account wants fewer\nconfiguration options exposed (\"too many knobs\"), while another explicitly\nwants more fine-grained controls per project. This investigation consolidates\nthe feedback behind HLR-1, determines which direction (or combination) takes\nprecedence, and records a decision that gates all administration-usability\nimplementation work on the Dashboard.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Consolidate the enterprise account feedback behind HLR-1: sources, quotes,\n  and the weight each account carries.\n- Inventory the current administration/configuration surface of the Dashboard\n  as context — per-component feature flags and defaults are administered\n  through the OdhDashboardConfig CR today.\n- Decide the direction for administration usability. The bounded outcomes are:\n  - **A — Simplify**: reduce and consolidate the configuration options exposed\n    to administrators, backing them with sane defaults.\n  - **B — Fine-grained controls**: add per-project administrative control\n    granularity.\n  - **Layered**: simplified defaults for the common path plus advanced\n    per-project controls (both outcomes apply).\n- Record the decision (ADR or equivalent decision document) with rationale,\n  the affected administration surfaces, and the selected outcome label.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A consolidated feedback summary exists that names the conflicting\n  requirements, their account sources, and the precedence rule applied.\n- A decision document records the selected outcome (A, B, or layered) with\n  rationale and identifies which Dashboard administration surfaces are\n  affected.\n- The decision is agreed by the stakeholders who own the conflicting account\n  relationships.\n- The outcome is recorded in one of the bounded labels so the corresponding\n  implementation work can be planned immediately.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 — resolves the contradictory administration-usability feedback and\n  determines which implementation direction is pursued.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":39979,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8405694652183ce9","agent_id":"a84dc4f3fbe0fa09d","session_id":"18366dc2-8783-4e47-973f-83e0b584ee1e","uuid":"be0ee953-6e3a-4692-93b8-61678c823ecc","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:38:25.667Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9008"}
