{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b32c6d825e4cc9b2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9008-E001\n3\ttitle: Resolve conflicting administration-usability direction\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9008\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 0\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Resolve conflicting administration-usability direction for enterprise accounts\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tHLR-1 asks that \"administration should be simpler\", but the consolidated\n30\taccount feedback is directly contradictory: one strategic account wants fewer\n31\tconfiguration options exposed (\"too many knobs\"), while another explicitly\n32\twants more fine-grained controls per project. This investigation consolidates\n33\tthe feedback behind HLR-1, determines which direction (or combination) takes\n34\tprecedence, and records a decision that gates all administration-usability\n35\timplementation work on the Dashboard.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Consolidate the enterprise account feedback behind HLR-1: sources, quotes,\n40\t  and the weight each account carries.\n41\t- Inventory the current administration/configuration surface of the Dashboard\n42\t  as context — per-component feature flags and defaults are administered\n43\t  through the OdhDashboardConfig CR today.\n44\t- Decide the direction for administration usability. The bounded outcomes are:\n45\t  - **A — Simplify**: reduce and consolidate the configuration options exposed\n46\t    to administrators, backing them with sane defaults.\n47\t  - **B — Fine-grained controls**: add per-project administrative control\n48\t    granularity.\n49\t  - **Layered**: simplified defaults for the common path plus advanced\n50\t    per-project controls (both outcomes apply).\n51\t- Record the decision (ADR or equivalent decision document) with rationale,\n52\t  the affected administration surfaces, and the selected outcome label.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- A consolidated feedback summary exists that names the conflicting\n57\t  requirements, their account sources, and the precedence rule applied.\n58\t- A decision document records the selected outcome (A, B, or layered) with\n59\t  rationale and identifies which Dashboard administration surfaces are\n60\t  affected.\n61\t- The decision is agreed by the stakeholders who own the conflicting account\n62\t  relationships.\n63\t- The outcome is recorded in one of the bounded labels so the corresponding\n64\t  implementation work can be planned immediately.\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability\n67\t\n68\t- HLR-1 — resolves the contradictory administration-usability feedback and\n69\t  determines which implementation direction is pursued.\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a3d582ee432abf1","agent_id":"a718e3aea7ece3ad9","session_id":"18366dc2-8783-4e47-973f-83e0b584ee1e","uuid":"2450ad1e-a848-4e89-8944-23ea9a068ca8","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:44:36.850Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b32c6d825e4cc9b2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9008 decomposition"}
