{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c4ffb02e4c9a210","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9008-E002\n3\ttitle: Define data-scientist onboarding scope and time baseline\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9008\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 0\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -2\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Define data-scientist onboarding scope and time baseline\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tHLR-2 requires that onboarding a new data scientist take \"less than a day\",\n30\tbut the strategy does not define what onboarding includes or where the day is\n31\tcurrently spent. This investigation defines the onboarding scope, baselines\n32\tthe current time-to-onboard, and identifies the friction points — the output\n33\tdetermines what onboarding implementation work exists and where it lands.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Define what \"onboarding a new data scientist\" covers. Candidate stages named\n38\t  in the strategy: cluster access, project setup, first workbench, first\n39\t  deployed model. Determine which are in scope and in what order.\n40\t- Baseline the current onboarding journey: where elapsed time and friction\n41\t  actually occur today for each in-scope stage (Dashboard-side project\n42\t  creation and workbench spawn, Notebooks-side workbench lifecycle and image\n43\t  readiness, and any environment/access steps).\n44\t- Produce a prioritized list of friction points with the responsible surface\n45\t  (Dashboard vs. Notebooks vs. out of product scope).\n46\t- Record the scope decision so downstream implementation work can be planned;\n47\t  explicitly call out whether the workbench experience is in scope.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- The onboarding scope is defined: which candidate stages are included, with\n52\t  a stated rationale.\n53\t- A current-state baseline exists showing where time is spent across the\n54\t  in-scope stages.\n55\t- Friction points are identified, prioritized, and mapped to the surface that\n56\t  owns each.\n57\t- The scope decision explicitly states whether Notebooks-side workbench work\n58\t  is included, since that determines whether a Notebooks implementation epic\n59\t  exists.\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- HLR-2 — converts the undefined \"onboarding in less than a day\" requirement\n64\t  into a defined scope and baseline that implementation work can target.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a3d582ee432abf1","agent_id":"a718e3aea7ece3ad9","session_id":"18366dc2-8783-4e47-973f-83e0b584ee1e","uuid":"89bd7a08-054c-471a-ae65-2ee1e3585d36","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:44:37.993Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c4ffb02e4c9a210","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9008 decomposition"}
