 finding that no actionable tooling\n48\t  requirement exists (in which case HLR-3 is closed as not actionable).\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- A consolidated list of specific enterprise tools is produced from the\n53\t  account feedback, with the expecting account named for each.\n54\t- Each listed tool has a stated integration expectation and a candidate\n55\t  integration surface in the platform.\n56\t- The list is prioritized and validated with the stakeholders who own the\n57\t  account relationships.\n58\t- The investigation closes with either an actionable tool list or an explicit\n59\t  not-actionable finding — it does not end with an open question.\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- HLR-3 — converts the unspecified \"integrate better with enterprise tooling\"\n64\t  requirement into a concrete, prioritized tool list that implementation work\n65\t  can target.\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a3d582ee432abf1","agent_id":"a718e3aea7ece3ad9","session_id":"18366dc2-8783-4e47-973f-83e0b584ee1e","uuid":"d753ff1d-758a-4961-a431-456ca8956365","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:44:38.972Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-982fc430ec948d4c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9008 decomposition"}
