n experience\n50\t  the scope decision calls for.\n51\t- Address the Dashboard-side friction points identified in the onboarding\n52\t  baseline, in priority order.\n53\t- Keep scope strictly consistent with the defined onboarding scope; anything\n54\t  the scope decision excludes is out of scope here.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- A new data scientist can complete every in-scope onboarding stage that has a\n59\t  Dashboard surface, end to end, through the Dashboard.\n60\t- The Dashboard-side steps identified in the friction baseline are addressed\n61\t  or explicitly dispositioned.\n62\t- The measured time for the Dashboard-side portion of onboarding supports the\n63\t  overall \"less than a day\" target for the defined scope.\n64\t- Existing project and workbench management functionality is unaffected by\n65\t  regression.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- HLR-2 — delivers the Dashboard-side portion of onboarding a new data\n70\t  scientist in less than a day.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a3d582ee432abf1","agent_id":"a718e3aea7ece3ad9","session_id":"18366dc2-8783-4e47-973f-83e0b584ee1e","uuid":"ff12168f-4b75-4be1-84f8-ca63743b5735","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:44:44.147Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-88c55beec597cf71","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9008 decomposition"}
