m workbench\n51\t  spawn to usable state, image selection and readiness behavior).\n52\t- Preserve existing workbench lifecycle behavior: culling defaults and\n53\t  per-workbench overrides continue to be administered through the Dashboard,\n54\t  and OAuth sidecar behavior is unchanged.\n55\t- Keep scope strictly consistent with the defined onboarding scope.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- A new data scientist's first workbench reaches a usable state within the\n60\t  expectation set by the defined onboarding scope.\n61\t- The Notebooks-side friction points identified in the onboarding baseline\n62\t  are addressed or explicitly dispositioned.\n63\t- Existing workbench lifecycle behavior (culling, OAuth sidecars, per-workbench\n64\t  overrides) is unaffected by regression.\n65\t- If the defined onboarding scope does not include the workbench experience,\n66\t  this epic is removed rather than forced — that outcome is recorded by the\n67\t  scope definition, not here.\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- HLR-2 — delivers the Notebooks-side portion of onboarding a new data\n72\t  scientist in less than a day.\n73\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a3d582ee432abf1","agent_id":"a718e3aea7ece3ad9","session_id":"18366dc2-8783-4e47-973f-83e0b584ee1e","uuid":"4bbdede3-8017-4c8e-958e-2736c7f39439","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:44:45.390Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-899818b391c52037","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9008 decomposition"}
